  "description": "HUJWIU crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C99 H189 Cu3 O55 P6 Tb9,C8 H12 Cu1 N4. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.436-4.303 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.43-122.77°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cu(MeCN)4][Cu3Tb9(μ3-OH)7(O3PtBu)6(O2CtBu)15]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 7 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
